Title: Title-only requests lost the Sci-Hub title search
Created: 2026-10-29
Author: MinhHaDuong

--- log ---
2026-10-29T20:59Z MinhHaDuong created

2026-10-29T21:02Z note Author ruling 2026-10-29: option (a), title kind
--- body ---
## Context

Found by the integration review of tracker 0008 (raid f9e483). Before 0019, Sci-Hub searched by title
when a record had no DOI (249fee1 `scihub.py:90`: `build_query_urls(doi, safe_title)`). The contract has
no title kind: title-only rows become `Request("doi", "", path)` (`cli.py:244-256`) and Sci-Hub now
builds `build_query_urls(doi, "")` (`scihub.py:78`), an empty search
(`build_query_urls("", "")[:1] == ['https://sci-hub.fr/?s=']`). No test covered the old behaviour.

## Decision for the author
- (a) Add a `title` kind to the contract; Sci-Hub (and any other source that can search by title)
  lists it in `ACCEPTS`. Restores the feature; small contract change (~1-2 USD agent).
- (b) Drop title-only fetching: reject title-only rows with a clear error, fix `--title` help text and
  README. Simplest (~0.5 USD agent).

## Exit criteria
- [ ] The chosen option is implemented and a test pins it (title-only input either searches by title
      on a source that accepts it, or fails with a clear message)
